      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Shepherd\u2019s Flock are a cult devoted to Maelthor, acting to advance his influence and emergence while believing their actions purify the world and secure human supremacy.\n\nThe Shepherd\u2019s Flock are explicitly identified as a cult (Claim 2) that follows and aligns with Maelthor (Claims 3\u20134). Their ideology frames their actions as cleansing impurities that resist Maelthor\u2019s influence (Claim 5), and they justify these acts as necessary sacrifices for a greater good (Claim 6). They also pursue a goal of ensuring human supremacy (Claim 7).\n\nThey are active and organized: recruiting\u2014especially transformed individuals\u2014by offering purpose and revealing truths about those transformations (Claims 8\u201311), and publicly staging protests at city gates with vocal members (Claims 12\u201315). They also obscure or manipulate events, presenting incidents as defensive tragedies (Claim 20).\n\nNo contradictions appear in the provided claims.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Nature: Cult (Shepherd\u2019s Flock)\n- Allegiance: Maelthor (deity/power)\n- Beliefs: World purification, justified sacrifice, human supremacy\n- Activities: Recruitment, protests, narrative control\n- Symbol: Exists; found on guards\u2019 bodies\n- Methods: Includes hiding corrupted meat, targeted recruitment",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_the_city_council_2",
      "question": "Who speaks for the wizards on the council, and what's his angle on the cult?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
