      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright, a gnome, speaks for the wizards on the council, and he\u2019s aggressively proactive\u2014treating the cult as a serious arcane threat and pushing detection, containment, and countermeasures.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright represents the Arcane and speaks for the Wizard\u2019s College on the council. His angle on the cult is uncompromising: he takes any threat to the city seriously and views the cult\u2019s corrupted meat as a perversion of magic. He is eager to deploy the College\u2019s resources to detect and counteract the cult\u2019s influence, plans to magically lock the city down, and intends to use a rune to identify corrupted meat. He will be the first to present his plan, signaling urgency and leadership in responding to a cult associated with dark magic, operating below the city, and attempting to reach the city\u2019s heart.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Headmaster of the Wizard\u2019s College; council representative for the Arcane  \n- Species: Gnome  \n- Stance: Treats cult as serious threat; sees corruption as magical perversion  \n- Actions/Plans: City lockdown via magic; rune to detect corrupted meat; rapid deployment of College resources  \n- Context: Cult uses hidden routes below the city; influence is active and being countered",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
