      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The outcome is contradictory\u2014PREP/OBSERVED facts show the Wolf both escaping and being killed; the most terminal state given is that the Wolf is \u201cdecapitated\u201d and \u201chead is removed from the body,\u201d but this conflicts with escape outcomes.\n\nThere are two incompatible outcomes in the projection:\n\n- OBSERVED/PREP: The Wolf \u201cattempts to escape via a secret tunnel,\u201d \u201cattempts to flee,\u201d \u201cbecame invisible,\u201d and \u201cescaped or attempted to escape.\u201d This supports a surviving, fleeing Wolf.\n- OBSERVED (terminal): Bonogo \u201cremoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it,\u201d and the Wolf is explicitly \u201cdecapitated\u201d and \u201chead is removed from the body.\u201d These are terminal outcomes and imply death.\n\nBecause terminal outcomes take precedence for continuity, the strongest current state is that the Wolf is dead (decapitated), unless your table has not yet resolved that moment in play. If both appeared in different branches, you\u2019ll need to choose which version is canon going forward.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Identity: The Wolf (cultist, second-in-command of the guard)\n- Status: Conflicted \u2014 escaped vs. \u201cdecapitated\u201d\n- Abilities: Illusions, invisibility, deception\n- Location: Council chamber during the battle\n- Opposition: Bonogo (bugbear) who carried out the killing blow (decapitation)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
