      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no information in the provided context about Thalia\u2019s reliability or behavior in the meeting, so you can\u2019t determine if she\u2019s trustworthy or compromised.\n\nThe projection includes multiple references to Thalia (e.g., Caelynn giving her instructions, Stafl attacking her after being revived), but none describe her demeanor, allegiance, or any suspicious traits during the emergency meeting. There are also no indicators like corruption (e.g., \u201coily sheen to their eyes\u201d) or faction ties tied to Thalia specifically.\n\nGiven how often corruption, charm effects, and hidden agendas are explicitly noted for others (e.g., guards, Bonogo, Stafl), the absence of such flags for Thalia means there\u2019s simply not enough evidence either way.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Presence in events: Received instructions from Caelynn; interacted with party members\n- Behavioral indicators: Not specified\n- Corruption/suspicion markers: None provided\n- Meeting relevance: No direct facts about her conduct in the emergency meeting",
