        "summoning": "retriever_gap",
        "consequences": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: If the council stalls, the city slides closer to disaster\u2014cult plans advance, coordinated attacks continue, and threats like tainted meat, infrastructure sabotage, and the flesh kaiju summoning go unchecked.\n\nThe projection is clear that inaction has compounding consequences. Each \u201cfailed or unresolved council debate\u201d brings the city \u201ccloser to disaster\u201d (CANON). Meanwhile, the cult is actively operating below the city, attempting to \u201ccomplete a summoning ritual\u201d for a flesh kaiju and \u201caccess the heart of the city\u201d (CANON). They can also \u201csabotage or corrupt cauldrons,\u201d worsening the tainted meat crisis the council is already debating (CANON).\n\nAt the same time, \u201ccoordinated attacks occur across the city\u201d and the \u201ccity\u2019s stability is threatened by the cult\u201d (CANON). Infrastructure risks escalate too\u2014hidden passages and tunnels allow movement, and sealing them could \u201crisk isolation\u201d of city sections (CANON). Add in unrest from the steep toll and protests, and the situation destabilizes further.\n\nNo conflicting claims here: all sources align that delay strengthens the cult and weakens the city.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Threats: cult summoning ritual, tainted meat, coordinated attacks, centipede risk  \n- Political state: ongoing council debate, influence from cult within council  \n- Infrastructure: tunnels, sewers, risk of isolation if sealed  \n- Public unrest: protests over high toll  \n- Stakes: city moving toward disaster with inaction",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_arch_current",
      "question": "What does the Council Room look like after the wolf fight-what should we notice?",
