      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room is tense, partially secured, and full of uneasy guards\u2014evidence of chaos remains, and there\u2019s a major contradiction: the Wolf both \u201cescaped while invisible during the encounter\u201d and \u201cwas decapitated and had his head removed from his body,\u201d so you\u2019ll need to decide which outcome is current.\n\nAfter the fight, the large circular Council Room is still ringed by guards (8 regular, 2 elite), many visibly corrupted with an oily sheen in their eyes. Guards are tense, trying to maintain order while alarms outside keep others from entering. Some guards may be benefiting from nearby corrupted meat (temporary HP), adding to the unease.\n\nThe space likely shows signs of confusion and disruption tied to the Wolf\u2019s tactics\u2014illusion-based misdirection and panic. The players would remember being disoriented by duplicates, and that atmosphere lingers in how NPCs behave.\n\nA key environmental detail is the secret passage beneath the chamber, which the Wolf used when he \u201cattempted to escape through a secret passage beneath the council chamber.\u201d\n\nConflict note: OBSERVED facts state both that the Wolf \u201cescaped while invisible during the encounter\u201d and that he \u201cwas decapitated and had his head removed from his body.\u201d These are mutually exclusive terminal outcomes; the current state depends on which event the GM treats as canon.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Guards in a ring formation; corrupted presence among them\n- Atmosphere: Tense, disbelieving, controlled chaos\n- Notable Features: Secret passage beneath chamber; active lockdown outside\n- Threat Indicators: Corruption (oily sheen eyes), lingering illusion confusion",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
