      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Chambers were heavily disrupted\u2014hit by a Fireball, triggering defensive runes, and left disheveled with active magical effects like illusory walls.\n\nDuring Session 12 (OBSERVED):\n- The room was dramatically affected by magic: \u201calmost the entire room is lit up by Fireball,\u201d indicating a major destructive or disruptive spell event.\n- The chamber\u2019s defenses reacted: \u201crunes along the walls activated when Caelynn cast her spell,\u201d confirming active magical ward responses.\n- Illusory elements were in play: \u201cIllusory Walls are present in portions of the room,\u201d contributing to confusion and altered battlefield conditions.\n- The space is now in a degraded state: physical_condition is \u201cDisheveled.\u201d\n- Reinforcements are shifting the scene: \u201cguards are being drawn here as reinforcements,\u201d escalating tension and activity.\n\nNo conflicting states are present; all details consistently indicate the chamber transitioned from a formal deliberation space into an active, magically disrupted combat zone.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: Disheveled  \n- Defenses: Activated runes, illusory walls, ancient wards  \n- Atmosphere: Fireball-lit, tense, chaotic  \n- Operational Changes: Guards converging on the chamber",
