      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is most likely dead\u2014he \u201cwas decapitated\u201d and his \u201chead was removed from his body\u201d\u2014but this conflicts with claims that he \u201cescapes\u201d while invisible, so there\u2019s a continuity issue to resolve.\n\nThere are two incompatible outcomes in the record:\n- Terminal outcome: The Wolf \u201cwas decapitated\u201d and his \u201chead was removed from his body\u201d (reinforced by Bonogo removing the head to transport it). These are definitive death indicators.\n- Escape outcome: The Wolf \u201cescapes\u201d after becoming invisible and attempting to flee via the secret passage.\n\nBecause decapitation is a terminal condition, it overrides non-terminal escape unless the escape occurred earlier in the sequence or involved a duplicate/illusion (which he can create). The presence of illusions and invisibility introduces ambiguity but does not negate the explicit terminal phrasing.\n\nState assessment:\n- Physical state: Dead (per terminal outcome).\n- Corruption: Previously corrupted (cultist, saboteur), but moot if dead.\n- Continuity issue: Escape vs. death needs timeline clarification.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Cultist, saboteur, second-in-command of the guard\n- Abilities: Invisibility, illusory duplicates, deception/persuasion\n- Status in session: Central adversary, confronted in council chamber battle",
      "embedding_similarity": null
