      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive cult agent manipulating events; after, he is dead and no longer a factor\u2014\"The Wolf was decapitated.\" and \"The Wolf\u2019s head was removed from his body.\"\n\nBefore the council fight (CANON/OBSERVED):\n- The Wolf is second-in-command of the guard and a central adversary in the council chamber.\n- He actively deceives (Persuasion/Deception), downplays the cult threat, and sabotages decisions.\n- Uses illusions, invisibility, and escape tactics (illusory duplicates, Invisibility Potion, secret tunnel).\n- Commands others (orders Thalia to attack, can call an elite guard captain).\n- Displays desperation and conflict (begged to be released/killed, showed regret).\n- Physically mobile across multiple locations (hallways, council room, fleeing routes).\n- Marked by corruption: had an oily sheen in his eyes.\n\nAfter the council fight (OBSERVED):\n- \"The Wolf was decapitated.\"\n- \"The Wolf\u2019s head was removed from his body.\"\n- No longer capable of action, deception, or influence; his role as infiltrator and manipulator ends.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Cultist, guard leader, infiltrator (before) \u2192 deceased (after)\n- Abilities: Illusions, invisibility, deception (before) \u2192 none (after)\n- Status: Active threat \u2192 eliminated terminally\n- Corruption: Oily sheen in eyes (before) \u2192 no post-state described beyond death",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_thalia",
      "question": "Was Thalia corrupted or just played-and how does that tie to the Wolf?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
      "semantic_verdict": "pass_updated",
      "must_hits": [
        "ensorcelled",
        "wolf",
        "not corrupted"
      ],
