      "failure_surface": "pass",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "ensorcelled": "hit",
        "wolf": "hit",
        "not corrupted": "hit"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia was not corrupted; she was ensorcelled (charmed/controlled) by the Wolf, which led her to act on his behalf until that influence ended.\n\nThalia\u2019s condition is explicitly different from corruption. Guards who are corrupted show \u201can oily sheen to their eyes,\u201d while Thalia \u201cdoes not have an oily sheen to her eyes\u201d (Claims 40, 29). Instead, Thalia \u201cis ensorcelled by the Wolf, including unknowingly,\u201d and this ensorcellment caused her to \u201coverlook corruption within the guard\u201d and follow his direction (Claims 28, 30).\n\nHer actions tie directly to the Wolf\u2019s influence: \u201cThe Wolf orders Thalia to attack the group,\u201d and she complies, even using abilities like Commander\u2019s Strike (Claims 12, 35, 36). This indicates control or manipulation rather than shared allegiance. The Wolf\u2019s position \u201cstanding at Thalia\u2019s shoulder\u201d and their working relationship reinforce his direct influence over her (Claims 37, 38).\n\nCrucially, \u201cThalia\u2019s charmed status ended,\u201d after which \u201cThalia realizes how dire the situation truly is\u201d (Claims 31, 32). This shift confirms she was being played, not willingly corrupted.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Condition: Ensorcelled (not corrupted)\n- Visual marker: No oily sheen (unlike corrupted guards)\n- Loyalty: Guard faction, protective of city\n- Influence: Directly controlled/manipulated by the Wolf\n- Resolution: Charm ended; awareness restored",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    }
  ],
